OPTIONAL Structure 4: Spring into Action by Jeff Beynon
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aul0SzPVsls

This structure was folded but the mechanism of which was not possible to create a moving compoenent within the provided timeframe. An A4 paper is used in the video but the model variation created for the Kalidescope of emotions used 7 divisions not 12. Measure the width of the peice used and create 7 divisions instead of 12. For the length ways 6 divisions were made. This allows for a simpler model that can be used to model a mechanism around easier. The idea behind using this origami structure was to have it expand to its full state using something similar to the robot arm. Applying pressure at the middle of the structure in a gripping pinching motion allows for expansion. 

















